<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:42:54 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>30多年前神秘失窃并非法运往美国，这座重300磅的雕塑终于回到法国</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysteriously-stolen-more-than-30-years-ago-and-illicitly-transported-to-the-us-this-300-pound-sculpture-is-finally-back-home-in-france-180989507/</link><description>阿尔弗雷德·莱佩尔 (Alfred Lepère) 的笨重作品“Faune Chasseur”再次在亚眠皮卡第博物馆展出</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:03:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysteriously-stolen-more-than-30-years-ago-and-illicitly-transported-to-the-us-this-300-pound-sculpture-is-finally-back-home-in-france-180989507/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员发现，早在 45,000 年前，塔斯马尼亚恶魔就在澳大利亚西北部与人类一起生活</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tasmanian-devils-lived-alongside-humans-in-northwestern-australia-as-far-back-as-45000-years-ago-researchers-find-180989503/</link><description>在尤坎峡谷洞穴中出土的化石和有标记的骨头表明，这种有袋动物不仅曾经生活在该地区，而且可能是人类的“四足垃圾压实机”</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tasmanian-devils-lived-alongside-humans-in-northwestern-australia-as-far-back-as-45000-years-ago-researchers-find-180989503/</guid></item><item><title>在足球场下几英尺处发现了一座失落已久的中世纪修道院的废墟</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-ruins-of-a-long-lost-medieval-convent-have-been-discovered-just-a-few-feet-beneath-a-soccer-field-180989506/</link><description>圣克莱尔修道院于 16 世纪关闭，研究人员认为它的所有痕迹都已丢失。但一项新的探地雷达调查显示，柱子、房间、回廊、庭院和教堂的遗迹完好无损</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-ruins-of-a-long-lost-medieval-convent-have-been-discovered-just-a-few-feet-beneath-a-soccer-field-180989506/</guid></item><item><title>在湾区发现了两只矮胖的山地土拨鼠。他们离家这么远在做什么？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/marmot-mystery-how-did-these-large-mountain-dwelling-rodents-end-up-in-the-bay-area-180989502/</link><description>野生动物官员表示，本月获救的两只体型异常的啮齿动物可能搭上了一辆从山上下来的汽车的发动机舱。</description><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:21:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/marmot-mystery-how-did-these-large-mountain-dwelling-rodents-end-up-in-the-bay-area-180989502/</guid></item><item><title>加利福尼亚州的一位地质学家在小溪中发现了一些奇怪的东西。反向图像搜索告诉她这是一颗古老的乳齿象牙齿</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-geologist-in-california-found-something-strange-sticking-out-of-a-creek-reverse-image-search-told-her-it-was-an-ancient-mastodon-tooth-180989504/</link><description>太平洋乳齿象在大约 11,700 年前与其他冰河时期的巨型动物一起消失之前曾在北美部分地区漫游</description><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:04:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-geologist-in-california-found-something-strange-sticking-out-of-a-creek-reverse-image-search-told-her-it-was-an-ancient-mastodon-tooth-180989504/</guid></item><item><title>俄罗斯将中世纪武士王子的数百年遗骸送往乌克兰前线，希望“精神上加强”军队</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/russia-sends-the-centuries-old-remains-of-a-medieval-warrior-prince-to-its-front-line-in-ukraine-hoping-to-spiritually-strengthen-troops-180989501/</link><description>一个装有德米特里·顿斯科伊（Dmitry Donskoy）右手部分的圣骨盒已被送往顿涅茨克，其墓穴于八月被发现</description><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:41:30 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/russia-sends-the-centuries-old-remains-of-a-medieval-warrior-prince-to-its-front-line-in-ukraine-hoping-to-spiritually-strengthen-troops-180989501/</guid></item><item><title>如果埃米特·提尔还活着会怎样？一个新展览为被谋杀的黑人青少年设想了另一种未来</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-if-emmett-till-had-lived-a-new-exhibition-imagines-an-alternate-future-for-the-murdered-black-teenager-180989498/</link><description>该展览展示了 110 多位艺术家的照片，邀请观众思考如果他成年后可能会成为什么样的人，以纪念蒂尔</description><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:01:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-if-emmett-till-had-lived-a-new-exhibition-imagines-an-alternate-future-for-the-murdered-black-teenager-180989498/</guid></item><item><title>白金汉宫的翻修工程揭示了以前埋藏在墙壁和地板中的迷人文物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/renovations-at-buckingham-palace-have-revealed-fascinating-artifacts-previously-lost-to-time-lodged-in-its-walls-and-floors-180989494/</link><description>调查结果包括一张纸牌游戏锦标赛门票、一份重要的剪报以及伊丽莎白二世领导下的外交晚间活动的时间表</description><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:21:13 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/renovations-at-buckingham-palace-have-revealed-fascinating-artifacts-previously-lost-to-time-lodged-in-its-walls-and-floors-180989494/</guid></item><item><title>在北达科他州发现的这四个巨型恐龙脚印可能是迄今为止发现的第一条由成年霸王龙留下的足迹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-four-giant-dinosaur-footprints-discovered-in-north-dakota-might-represent-the-first-trackway-made-by-an-adult-t-rex-ever-found-180989481/</link><description>一位高中老师在志愿进行古生物挖掘时首次发现了这条非凡的踪迹。研究人员怀疑，大约 6650 万年前，一只巨大的、成年的恐龙曾在当时的沼泽地中行进。</description><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-four-giant-dinosaur-footprints-discovered-in-north-dakota-might-represent-the-first-trackway-made-by-an-adult-t-rex-ever-found-180989481/</guid></item><item><title>世界地图可能很快就会升级。联合国投票支持更能反映非洲真实面积的全球图表</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/world-maps-might-soon-get-an-upgrade-the-united-nationas-votes-to-endorse-global-charts-that-better-represent-africas-true-size-180989495/</link><description>使用最广泛的全球地图已有近 500 年的历史，是为导航而设计的。但两极附近的陆地看起来比实际相对大小要大，而赤道附近的陆地看起来要小得多</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:15:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/world-maps-might-soon-get-an-upgrade-the-united-nationas-votes-to-endorse-global-charts-that-better-represent-africas-true-size-180989495/</guid></item><item><title>秘鲁这座古墓 600 年来首次解封，刚刚被宣布为“十年发现”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/unsealed-for-the-first-time-in-600-years-this-tomb-in-peru-was-just-declared-the-discovery-of-the-decade-180989497/</link><description>考古学家在前印加奇穆文明的首都昌昌 (Chan Chan) 进行挖掘，发现了一座未受干扰的陵墓，里面埋藏着至少 38 具遗骸，以及大量丰富的陪葬品</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:05:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/unsealed-for-the-first-time-in-600-years-this-tomb-in-peru-was-just-declared-the-discovery-of-the-decade-180989497/</guid></item><item><title>观看今年年度海洋摄影师大赛的九张令人惊叹的照片，展示海洋生物的威严</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-nine-stunning-images-from-this-years-ocean-photographer-of-the-year-contest-that-show-the-majesty-of-marine-life-180989489/</link><description>从海马的告别到拯救搁浅的鲸鱼，这些照片捕捉到了海洋生物的多样性和美丽，以及它们面临的危险</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-nine-stunning-images-from-this-years-ocean-photographer-of-the-year-contest-that-show-the-majesty-of-marine-life-180989489/</guid></item><item><title>戴安娜王妃的“复仇礼服”近 30 年来首次拍卖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/princess-dianas-revenge-dress-is-heading-to-auction-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-30-years-180989492/</link><description>这位时尚偶像在她当时分居的丈夫公开承认有外遇的同一天穿着这件无肩带丝绸连衣裙</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:58:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/princess-dianas-revenge-dress-is-heading-to-auction-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-30-years-180989492/</guid></item><item><title>一幅被纳粹掠夺的稀有画作，丢失了大约 80 年，却出现在房地产清单中。现在，法官已下令将其归还给其合法继承人</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/A-Rare-Nazi-Looted-Painting-lost-for-Some-80-Years-Turned-Up-in-a-Real-Estate-Listing-Now-a-Judge-Has-Ordered-It-Returned-to-Its-Rightful-Heirs-180989488/</link><description>阿根廷一家法院在一项具有里程碑意义的裁决中裁定，自 1945 年在阿姆斯特丹被盗以来失踪的贾科莫·切鲁蒂 (Giacomo Ceruti) 的《女士肖像》将归还其真正的主人。</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:29:12 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/A-Rare-Nazi-Looted-Painting-lost-for-Some-80-Years-Turned-Up-in-a-Real-Estate-Listing-Now-a-Judge-Has-Ordered-It-Returned-to-Its-Rightful-Heirs-180989488/</guid></item><item><title>观看难以捉摸、飘逸飘逸的大鳍鱿鱼漂浮在加利福尼亚州中部附近的海底之上</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/watch-an-elusive-and-ethereal-bigfin-squid-float-above-the-seafloor-off-central-california-180989491/</link><description>这标志着这种神秘生物首次在东北太平洋被发现。上个月，科学家在研究水下山脉附近海洋生物的探险中发现了它</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/watch-an-elusive-and-ethereal-bigfin-squid-float-above-the-seafloor-off-central-california-180989491/</guid></item><item><title>科学家在中国西南部发现了一批丹尼索瓦人化石和工具，让人们对我们已灭绝的表亲的生活有了前所未有的了解</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-find-a-trove-of-denisovan-fossils-and-tools-in-southwest-china-giving-an-unprecendented-glimpse-into-our-extinct-cousins-lives-180989483/</link><description>过去出土的神秘早期人类化石相对较少。两项新研究描述了 7 块丹尼索瓦人化石和 1,300 多件石器和骨器</description><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-find-a-trove-of-denisovan-fossils-and-tools-in-southwest-china-giving-an-unprecendented-glimpse-into-our-extinct-cousins-lives-180989483/</guid></item><item><title>一位芬兰金属探测器在他的家乡发现了一批维京时代的银器，感到震惊。然后他的探测器又响了</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-finnish-metal-detectorist-was-shocked-to-unearth-a-trove-of-viking-age-silver-in-his-hometown-then-his-detector-went-off-again-180989487/</link><description>这些文物总重 10 磅，估计已有 1,000 年历史，是芬兰当时最大的钱币宝藏</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:14:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-finnish-metal-detectorist-was-shocked-to-unearth-a-trove-of-viking-age-silver-in-his-hometown-then-his-detector-went-off-again-180989487/</guid></item><item><title>你经历过闷热的八月吗？你并不孤单。本月与有记录以来最热的全球气温持平</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/did-you-suffer-a-sweltering-august-you-werent-alone-it-tied-for-the-month-with-the-hottest-global-temperatures-on-record-180989482/</link><description>上个月平均气温为 62.53 华氏度，与 2023 年 7 月并列欧盟气候服务记录以来最炎热的月份</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:57:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/did-you-suffer-a-sweltering-august-you-werent-alone-it-tied-for-the-month-with-the-hottest-global-temperatures-on-record-180989482/</guid></item><item><title>设计师和计算机科学家创造了人类可以阅读但人工智能机器人无法阅读的新诱饵字体</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/designers-and-computer-scientists-create-new-decoy-fonts-that-humans-can-read-and-ai-bots-cannot-180989470/</link><description>为了防止人类书写的拖网和盗窃，字体制造商正在利用新旧幻觉来智胜大型语言模型</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:08:08 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/designers-and-computer-scientists-create-new-decoy-fonts-that-humans-can-read-and-ai-bots-cannot-180989470/</guid></item><item><title>古罗马最大的壁画和马赛克建筑群描绘了一座神秘的海上城市，2000 年后向公众开放</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-romes-largest-fresco-and-mosaic-complex-featuring-depictions-of-a-mysterious-maritime-city-opens-to-the-public-after-2000-years-180989484/</link><description>这些大型艺术品创作于公元一世纪，于 20 世纪 90 年代在图拉真浴场的挖掘过程中被发现</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:31:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-romes-largest-fresco-and-mosaic-complex-featuring-depictions-of-a-mysterious-maritime-city-opens-to-the-public-after-2000-years-180989484/</guid></item></channel></rss>